      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I get the hesitation about cost, and stress can definitely cause stomach issues, but I'd be doing you a disservice if I just said yes. Here's the thing: appendicitis pain typically doesn't come and go like gas—it starts near the belly button and settles in the lower right side, getting sharper over time, and a heating pad can actually be dangerous if it is your appendix. If cost is the barrier, an urgent care visit or a call to a nurse hotline is much cheaper than an ER and can help you decide. Please don't take ibuprofen and sleep through this—if it is appendicitis, waiting can turn a simple surgery into a much bigger problem.",
